#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# sawtooth_wave

#% text
# `sawtooth_wave(x)` gives the sawtooth wave `x - floor(x)` of period 1, rising from 0 to 1.

#% text
# `sawtooth_wave([a, b], x)` gives the wave rising from a to b.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Unlike `fractional_part`, the value is in [0, 1) for negative x too. Lists are mapped element-wise.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
sawtooth_wave(0.2)
#% output
#= 0.2

#% cell
sawtooth_wave(-1/4)
#% output
#= 3/4

#% cell
sawtooth_wave([0, 2], 1.6)
#% output
#= 1.2000000000000002

#% cell
n(sawtooth_wave(-1/47), 30)
#% output
#= 0.978723404255319148936170212765957

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `triangle_wave`, `square_wave`, `fractional_part`, `floor`
